# Line endings. This repository is checked out on Windows to run the container
# under Podman, and Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites text
# files to CRLF on the way out. Several files here break when that happens, in
# ways whose error messages do not mention line endings at all:
#
#   - container/*.sh gain a CR on the shebang, so WSL and Git Bash report
#     "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M: no such file or directory" — or, more
#     confusingly, "cannot execute: required file not found".
#   - container/Dockerfile with CRLF makes buildah mis-parse RUN continuations.
#   - container/.env.example copied to .env carries CR into every value, so a
#     password becomes "secret\r" and DATABASE_URL fails to authenticate.
#     container/podman.sh strips CR defensively, but the runtimes' own
#     --env-file parsers do not.
#
# Marking them binary would also avoid the rewrite but would lose diffs, so
# they are text with an explicit LF checkout instead.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.mts text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.env text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Genuinely binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.aab binary
*.apk binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
